; This tree cannot be resolved by npm without this setting. i18next 25.x and
; react-i18next 15.x both declare a peer of typescript ^5, and this project
; builds on typescript 6.
;
; CORRECTION 2026-09-03. The original text of this file claimed npm ci was
; unaffected because it installs from the lockfile and never re-resolves, and
; that the conflict had therefore stayed invisible. Both claims were wrong.
; frontend/Dockerfile had been passing the flag to its own npm ci since before
; this file existed, so the conflict was known. And the requirement is npm
; version dependent: measured on npm 10.9.7, a clean npm ci fails with ERESOLVE
; without this file; on npm 11.10.1 the same command succeeded before the file
; existed. Do not conclude from one green build that the setting is unnecessary.
;
; Scope: every install in this project reads this file, including the image
; build. frontend/Dockerfile copies it alongside the package files so that the
; image and a developer's machine obey one source instead of each carrying its
; own flag.
;
; Removal: i18next 26.x and react-i18next 17.x accept typescript 6. After that
; upgrade, delete this file and confirm that npm install and the image build
; both resolve unaided.
legacy-peer-deps=true
